t deaths reported in Tari District alone). The figures are not complete counts.\n- Pie chart 7 (Western Highlands 2010) and pie chart 8 (NCD 2010) give counts of violent crimes including \"murder + manslaughter\", but the pdftotext layout does not tie each number to its label, so they were not extracted.\n- Tried, nothing usable: RPNGC (no annual crime report found online); PNG NSO (no crime yearbook table found); ANU \"Sorcery Accusation-Related Violence in PNG, Part 4\" (In Brief 2017/31) gives shares of reported sorcery-violence incidents by province (e.g. Morobe 15%), not homicide counts, so it was not extracted; a news item on Enga gun-violence tracking data (ground.news, search snippet only, not opened).\n- Not tried for lack of time: health facility (NHIS) deaths by province; the INA / Lae and NCD crime victimisation surveys (2008).","unmatched":0,"shapes":{"shapes_ADM2.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen PNG ADM2","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/PNG/ADM2/geoBoundaries-PNG-ADM2.geojson","licence":"Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Intergovernmental Organisations (CC BY 3.0 IGO)","year":"2019"},"shapes_ADM1.geojson":{"source":"geoBoundaries gbOpen PNG ADM1","url":"https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries/raw/9469f09/releaseData/gbOpen/PNG/ADM1/geoBoundaries-PNG-ADM1.geojson","licence":"Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Intergovernmental Organisations (CC BY 3.0 IGO)","year":"2019"}}}